Required Aureolin QA coverage

The focused Aureolin suite must prove the ninth identity and full nine-racer field, including 1–4 local humans and correct remaining bot counts.

It must prove normal/armed switching for player one, bot, and local human; two-second switch cooldown; whiteout/morph behavior; preservation of world pose and unrelated meters; persistence through ordinary wreck/respawn; reset only at a new race; rejection while Mind Controlled, wrecked, finished, paused, or counting down.

It must verify racerModel() returns v_aureolin.PNG in normal form and vtm_aureolin.PNG in armed form, with independent measured hulls.

It must verify normal and armed source bounds, uniform sprite scaling, correct road size, transparent-source misses, solid-source hits, and positive/negative tilt hitbox accuracy.

It must verify the bullet begins at the real turret muzzle at multiple scales and tilts.

It must verify left and right rockets begin at their respective launcher mouths, are distinct points, and do not originate at the vehicle center.

It must verify armed form is mandatory for every weapon.

It must verify manual bullet fire rate is frame-rate independent and genuinely rapid.

It must verify downward mobile gesture starts firing, pointer release stops firing, upward gesture remains boost, horizontal gesture remains lane movement, and ordinary tap/double-tap behavior is preserved.

It must verify keyboard and controller equivalents, including multiple local seats.

It must verify bullet heat drain, passive recharge, hitting zero, overheat latch, inability to fire at partial recharge, and permission to resume only at exactly/full 100%.

It must verify ultimate activation fills the yellow meter and clears overheat.

It must verify ultimate bullets do not drain the yellow meter.

It must verify armed ultimate auto-fire works for player, bot, and local-human state without a held fire button.

It must verify normal-form Aureolin does not auto-fire in the ultimate.

It must verify Mind Control immediately stops manual fire, bot fire, ultimate auto-fire, and rocket salvo generation.

It must verify one bullet produces exactly one -0.10× stack, multiple bullets stack, independently expire, never create negative speed, compose with ordinary Slow/boost/ultimate/Cole-related generic pace logic correctly, clear on cleanse, and clear on wreck/new race.

It must verify ordinary bullet range and exact 2.00× ultimate bullet range.

It must verify bullets expire at their range even if nothing is hit.

It must verify rocket salvos contain exactly two rockets, one left and one right.

It must verify the 2.0-second rocket salvo cooldown and that rockets consume no yellow meter.

It must verify rockets are ultimate-only and armed-form-only.

It must verify dynamic target priority is the closest racer ahead by canonical race progress and changes when racers overtake each other while a rocket is already in flight.

It must verify rockets never reverse to a racer behind the owner.

It must verify rocket lifetime/self-destruction when no collision occurs.

It must verify each rocket removes exactly one half shield, including the expected total of two half-units if both rockets in one salvo hit the same ordinary target.

It must verify correct wreck behavior if rocket shield damage reaches zero.

It must verify both projectile types self-destruct/do nothing against ulting Flann.

It must verify both projectile types consume themselves and call Verdant’s canonical reveal behavior against ulting Verdant without slowing or damaging it.

