Final implementation standard

Do not stop once Aureolin “basically works.”

The finished feature must feel native to SEREN.

The normal and armed cars must be sized and collided from their real artwork. The muzzle and launchers must be measured, not guessed. Bullets must visibly leave the turret. The two rockets must visibly leave their respective bazookas. Weapon timing must not depend on FPS. Every player/bot/local-human route must use the same mechanics. Nine-car races must remain correctly laid out. Special ultimate interactions must be resolved before ordinary projectile effects. The yellow meter must work in both DOM and split-screen Canvas HUDs. Existing racers must retain their behavior.

Do not replace the provided Aureolin art, redraw the vehicles, or modify the four PNGs to make implementation easier.

Finish only when all existing tests plus the new Aureolin-focused tests pass and the code/documentation no longer contains stale eight-racer assumptions that affect gameplay or UI.
